The learner constructs the augmented matrix of an already-echelon, nonsingular three-variable system, eliminates entries above the third pivot, then above the second pivot, and reads the unique RREF or ordered solution. Tutorial f74e6075-9c2a-5495-ab21-470711559f2a explicitly prescribes R2:=R2-a23 R3, R1:=R1-a13 R3, R1:=R1-a12 R2 when the respective coefficient is nonzero, and states that RREF is unique. Tutorial ce056e74-9707-52d3-b172-483ca14e1f8f explains unit pivots and zeros above and below each pivot. Prerequisite Gaussian elimination supplies matrix construction and row operations; forward elimination, row swapping and singular cases are neighboring skills.

Practice uses one five-choice radio field, with matrix RREF (q-20594, q-20598), vector (q-20591), or text assignments (q-131586, q-20589). Three variables, full rank and upper triangular structure keep the assessed operation backward elimination. Unit pivots and small integers keep the easy workload to two or three row additions: every captured practice system has unit pivots. The lesson's nonunit pivot introduction is context, not an extra sampled practice stage. Only easy is supported; moderate and hard lack practice evidence. Original difficulty labels remain stored, including absent labels. No diagrams occur.

The answer-bearing assignment is which of the five distinct candidate triples solves the equations. No label, position, sign, extremum or coordinate frequency is mathematically mandated. Preserve the existing sampler: select the candidate role and nonzero-coefficient mask before coefficients, integer translation and scale; derive the RHS from that candidate. Each observed bank is a separate profile. Coordinatewise affine transforms of its complete triples are conservative authored extensions, not claims about historical misconception recipes. They preserve distinct candidates and the same elimination workload. Nonzero coefficients range from -5 to 5, translations from -5 to 5, and scale is 1 or 2. Original larger coefficients remain replayable. Eligible masks have all three upper entries nonzero or exactly one absent; q-131586 demonstrates absent a12 and q-131588 absent a23; the general algorithm explicitly supports skipping any zero. All five answer roles and four masks must remain exercisable within each restored practice profile. Correct positions are shuffled; the learner UI also orders choices.

Relevant counterfactuals change the selected solution while keeping the bank and coefficient matrix fixed, forcing RHS, final RREF, key and explanation to change. Changes to coefficients with a recomputed RHS preserve the solution while changing the displayed elimination. Probe these pairs, positions, extrema, coordinate-frequency and profile cues before and after shared delivery filtering. Recognizing z directly is legitimate partial elimination, not a reason to forbid valid simplifications. Inventory selection and learner history cannot be fully tested offline.

Review finding 6f947ef9d75ceb3ab20e is reproduced: q-20598 (af324f37-b688-5363-a6a2-fc8d79b31ad4), q-20589 (5eba1f2e-9d1f-5a78-8bbb-878c7c8cae0e), and e-4709 (de738faf-e020-5058-b6a5-48020212fbc4) all raise KeyError at seed 731 with replay=True. The construction defect is a hand-maintained registry without a completeness obligation against all captured target-KP cases. Restore both practice banks; add canonical replay as an evidence-only fieldless worked example, excluded from practice sampling. Do not invent a canonical answer bank. A source-driven regression must enumerate every captured case and compare visible systems, full banks, inferred unique keys and worked matrices, including the previously repaired cases.

q-20598 has solution (0,1,-3) and five captured RREF choices, all retained. q-20589 has solution (3,-3,1) by substitution but lacks a captured difficulty, key and worked solution. Its key and generated elimination explanation are explicitly inferred from equations and the tutorial, not recovered original fields. e-4709 has solution (2,1,-4) and a worked solution but no answer field or difficulty. Its replay preserves that response contract and is never eligible for learning. Retain the earlier correction for q-131590: its captured key references (0,-2,1), absent from its bank; equations and solution require the existing bank member (-6,1,1). Source wording and malformed captured TeX are normalized for the UI; mathematical source banks and operative solution stages are preserved.

